---
title: Saving a favourite — with and without JavaScript
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Signed-in user
    participant B as Chrome
    participant L as Laravel<br/>FavouriteController
    participant D as MariaDB

    U->>B: presses "Save recipe" on a recipe page
    alt JavaScript on — favourite-toggle.js
        B->>L: fetch() POST /recipes/healthy-pizza/favourite<br/>Accept: application/json, with the CSRF token
        L->>D: attach the recipe to the user's favourites (no duplicates)
        L-->>B: 200 {"is_favourite": true, "message": "Recipe saved to favourites."}
        B-->>U: button changes to "Remove" in place, message read out by screen readers
    else JavaScript off, or the fetch fails
        B->>L: ordinary form POST to the same address
        L->>D: attach the recipe to the user's favourites
        L-->>B: 302 back to the recipe, with a status message
        B-->>U: page reloads showing "Recipe saved to favourites."
    end
